  Imported:      2026-10-21
  License:       BSD-3-Clause WITH PCRE2-exception (src/vendor/pcre2/LICENCE.md);
                 sljit is BSD-2-Clause (src/vendor/pcre2/deps/sljit/LICENSE)
  Local patches: applied in this order, from tools/patches/pcre2/
                 0001-split-compile-error-texts.patch

src/vendor/pcre2/ is the files listed in tools/vendor/keep/pcre2.txt, copied
from the release tarball with their upstream layout, with exactly the patch
above applied. tools/vendor/manifest.tsv pins the archive and its digest,
which is the one GitHub publishes for the release asset; tools/vendor/verify
re-derives the tree from it and fails on any other difference.

Only the 8-bit library is imported: the 31 translation units that
NON-AUTOTOOLS-BUILD lists, their headers, and sljit, which
pcre2_jit_compile.c includes. Two files are renamed as that document
directs: src/pcre2.h.generic to src/pcre2.h, and src/pcre2_chartables.c.dist
to src/pcre2_chartables.c. config.h is not imported; the package's own is
src/pcre2-config/config.h. The 16-bit and 32-bit libraries share these
sources but are not built. The POSIX wrapper, pcre2grep, pcre2test,
pcre2_dftables, the fuzzers, testdata/, doc/ and the CMake, autotools,
Bazel and Zig builds are excluded.

0001-split-compile-error-texts.patch splits one string literal of about
5,700 characters into two, because clang -pedantic warns about a literal
over the 4,095 characters ISO C99 requires and R CMD check reports that
warning. No message or error number changes.

Updating: change the version, tag, commit, archive and archive_sha256
columns of tools/vendor/manifest.tsv, run tools/vendor/fetch, rebase any
patch that no longer applies, and compare src/config.h.generic of the new
release with src/pcre2-config/config.h. Then update this file, the version
asserted in tests/testthat/test-info.R, and inst/COPYRIGHTS, and run
tools/vendor/verify. It checks that all of them agree.
